type: software
title: "How fast can a driven Markov network oscillate? A four-state counterexample to the affine Karpelevich conjecture, and the exact dimension at which it fails"
version: 1.0.0-candidate
date-released: 2026-10-27
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23687327
authors:
  - name: Anonymous
license: CC0-1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ipitchford/affinity-karpelevich-threshold"
url: "https://evidencepress.org/releases/affinity-karpelevich-threshold/"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. Refutes Supplement Eq. (S3) of Xu, Kolchinsky, Delvenne and Ito (PRL 135, 257102, 2025): an integer four-state rate matrix has a rescaled eigenvalue outside the Karpelevich region; containment holds for at most three states and fails in every dimension n >= 4 (complete graphs); exact certificates for n = 5, 6. The single-cycle case remains open."
keywords:
  - Markov rate matrix
  - Karpelevich region
  - cycle affinity
  - stochastic thermodynamics
  - eigenvalue bounds
  - counterexample
  - resetting
  - exact certificate
